$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM threo-1-Benzhydryl-2-hydroxypropylpiperidine (Vb). To a solution of 29.2
mmol of magnesium bromide in 10 ml of ether obtained from 0.71 g (29.2
mmol) of magnesium and 5,5 g (29.3 mmol) of 1,2-dibromoethane was added
in one portion 0.14 g (3.68 mmol) of lithium aluminum hydride. After 5
min the mixture was cooled to -20°C and while stirring was added dropwise
within 5-10 min 1.5 g (4.9 mmol) of ketone IV in 10 ml of ether. The
mixture was warmed to room temperature within 30 min, and the solvent was
removed under reduced pressure. To the residue was slowly added at 0°C 25
ml of 2 N hydrochloric acid, and the reaction product was extracted into
dichloromethane (2x25 ml). The organic solution was washed with 10 ml of
20% aqueous ammonia and dried with sodium sulfate. Then the solvent was
distilled off in a vacuum. 1.43 g (95%) of a mixture of Va and Vb
alcohols in 1:9 ratio (according to 1H NMR spectrum). After
recrystallization of the alcohols mixture in hydrochloride form from
chloroform containing 4-5% of ethyl ether. 1.22 g (85%) of alcohol Vb.
erythro-1-Benzhydryl-2-hydroxypropylpiperidine (Va) Vb: IR spectrum
(CCl4): 3320 cm-1 (νO-H). 1H NMR spectrum (CDCl3, TMS) δ, ppm: 0.90 t
(3H, J 7 Hz), 0.96-1.36 m (3H), 1.40-1.90 m (5H), 2.54 d.d (1H, J 10, 5
Hz), 2.66-2.96 m (2H), 3.90 d.d.d (1H, J 11, 8, 2.5 Hz), 4.82 br.s (1H),
5.20 s (1H), 7.04- 7.34 m (6H), 7.34-7.54 m (4H). Found, %: C 81.45; H
8.82. C21H27NO. Calculated, %: C 81.51; H 8.79 Va: IR spectrum (CCl4):
3320 cm-1 (νO-H). 1H NMR spectrum (CDCl3, TMS) δ, ppm: 1.00 t (3H, J 7.5
Hz), 1.10-1.80 m (8H), 2.00-2.20 m (1H), 2.34- 2.64 m (2H), 2.80-2.96 m
(1H), 4.16-4.28 m (1H), 5.52 s (1H), 7.04-7.50 m (10H). Found, %: C
81.60; H 8.68. C21H27NO. Calculated, %: C 81.51; H 8.79
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective, optimization study, optimized on reducing agent
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
