$DATUM 67-56-1
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: 3.4 Representative procedure for the reduction
a 1 : 1 mixture of imine (1a) and aldehyde (2a) using Pd(OAc)2. In dry
methanol (5 mL) were added 5 mol% Pd(OAc)2, imine 1a (0.5 mmol), and
aldehyde 2a (0.5 mmol) successively at room temperature. The reaction
mixture was stirred at room temperature under hydrogen atmosphere
(pressure 10 bar) for 5 h. Later, the solution was filtered and filtrate
was evaporated to afford crude product, which was purified by silica gel
column chromatography using a 20 : 1 mixture of pet ether and ethyl
acetate as an eluent to give pure product.
N-(3,4-dimethoxyphenethyl)aniline (3f). Yield 36%. 3,4-dimethoxybenzyl
alcohol (4d). Yield 81%. Reactant: 1f, 2d. 3f: 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ
7.20-7.16 (t, J = 7.6 Hz, 2H), 6.92 (s, 2H), 6.83 (d, J = 8.4 Hz, 1H),
6.72 (t, J = 7.2 Hz, 2H), 6.51 (d, J = 7.2 Hz, 2H), 4.25 (s, 2H), 3.97
(bs, 1H) 3.87 (s, 6H). 4d: 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 6.93-6.83 (m, 3H),
4.63 (s, 2H), 3.89 (s, 3H), 3.88 (s, 3H), 1.78 (bs, 1H).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM chemoselective, reduction with nanoporous Au catalyst favors C=N bond
reduction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Exclusive Chemoselective Reduction of Imines in the Coexistence of
Aldehydes Using AuNPore Catalyst
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
