$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Reduction of (R)-4-Menthen-3-one (1) by
i-Bu2AlH. c) A solution of enone 1 (0.50 g, 3.3 mmol) in anhydrous CH2Cl2
or Et2O (50 mL) was treated dropwise (78, 0, or 25°C, Ar) with a solution
of i-Bu2AlH (1.6 mL, 73%) in toluene, stirred for 2 h, treated at these
same temperatures with cold H2O (7 mL), and stirred for 0.5 h. The
resulting precipitate was filtered off through a layer of Al2O3 (5 cm).
The organic layer was dried over Na2SO4 and evaporated. The residue was
analyzed by capillary GC.
(1R,5R)-5-Methyl-2-(1-methylethyl)cyclohex-2-en-1-ol (2a). Yield 79%; 2b.
Yield 79%. 2a: [α]D20 -31.5°(c 0.6, EtOH), [α]D24 - 32.0° (c 1.0, EtOH),
Rf 0.55 (PE:t-BuOMe, 2:1). IR spectrum (KBr, ν, cm-1): 1664 (C=C),
3048-3600 (O-H). PMR spectrum (300.13 MHz, CDCl3, δ, ppm, J/Hz): 0.82
(3H, d, J= 7.0, 5-CH3), 1.15 [3H, d, J= 6.7, CH(CH3)2], 1.19 [3H, d, J=
6.7, CH(CH3)2], 1.52 (1H, ddd, 2J= 11.3, 3J= 8.4, 3J= 2.0, Ha-6),
1.62-1.70 (1H, m, He-6), 1.62-1.75 (1H, m, Ha-4), 1.98-2.06 (1H, m, H-5),
2.18-2.20 (1H, m, He-4), 2.95 [1H, d, J= 6.7, CH(CH3)2], 4.57 (1H, dd,
2J= 5.4, 3J= 5.3, Ha-1), 4.80 (1H, br.s, OH), 5.48 (1H, dd, 2J= 5.4, 3J=
4.7, H-3).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM chemoselective, stereoselective, alternative preparation shown
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
