$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: In dry methanol (5 mL) were added imine 1a
(0.5 mmol), aldehyde 2a (0.5 mmol), and NaBH4 (0.6 mmol) successively at
room temperature under N2 atmosphere. The reaction mixture was stirred at
room temperature for 5 h. Later, the solution was diluted with water (10
mL) and extracted with EtOAc (3×10 mL). Collective organic layers were
evaporated to give crude product, which was purified by silica gel column
chromatography using a 20 : 1 mixture of pet ether and ethyl acetate as
an eluent to give pure product.
1-(4-(3-(2-methoxyphenyl)allylamino)phenyl)ethanone (10b). Yield 4%.
1-(4-(3-(2-methoxyphenyl)allylamino)phenyl)ethanol (11b). Yield 56%.
substrate 9b. 10b: 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.83 (dd, J1 = 7.0 Hz, J2 =
1.6 Hz, 2H), 7.40 (dd, J1 = 7.6 Hz, J2 = 1.6 Hz, 1H), 7. 25-7.21 (m, 1H),
6.96-6.86 (m, 3H), 6.63-6.61 (m, 2H), 6.30 (td, J1 = 16.0 Hz, J2 = 6.0
Hz), 4.40 (bs, 1H), 4.01 (dt, J1 = 6.0 Hz, J2 = 1.6 Hz, 2H), 3.84 (s,
3H), 2.50 (s, 3H); 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3) δ 196.4, 156.7, 152.0, 130.8,
128.9, 127.4, 127.0, 126.9, 126.2, 125.5, 120.7, 111.7, 110.9, 55.5,
46.0, 26.0; HRMS (ESI positive) calcd for C18H19NO2 [M + H]+: 282.1494,
found: 282.1486. 11b: 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.72-7.40 (m, 3H),
7.21-7.18 (m, 2H), 6.96-6.85 (m, 3H), 6.65 (d, J = 8.8 Hz, 1H), 6.33 (td,
J1 = 16.0 Hz, J2 = 6.0 Hz), 4.79 (q, J = 6.4 Hz, 1H), 3.93 (dd, J1 = 6.0
Hz, J2 = 1.2 Hz, 2H), 3.84 (s, 3H), 1.46 (d, J = 6.4 Hz, 3H); 13C NMR
(100 MHz, CDCl3) δ 147.7, 134.7, 132.3, 130.9, 128.8, 128.6, 127.6,
126.6, 125.9, 120.7, 113.0, 110.9, 70.2, 55.5, 46.8, 24.7; HRMS (ESI
nigative) calcd for C18H21NO2 [M - H]+: 282.1494, found: 282.1487.
